2f21f2551af82625cc0dcfee93da845c7a5acead","file":"preprints/Tensor-Saturation-for-Even-Spin-Groups-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":33,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1f74dede01672ba61b6610cef039e75a13554e835274f0e19a6afa92ca5b7c97","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Tensor-Saturation-for-Even-Spin-Groups-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:009565f440aab606fd47193a2f21f2551af82625cc0dcfee93da845c7a5acead","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Tensor-Saturation-for-Even-Spin-Groups-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L33"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $G=\\Spin(2n)$, $n\\ge2$, and let $\\lambda,\\mu,\\nu$ be dominant\nintegral weights such that $\\lambda+\\mu+\\nu\\in Q(D_n)$. Then, for every\npositive integer $N$,\n\\[\n \\bigl(V(\\lambda)\\otimes V(\\mu)\\otimes V(\\nu)\\bigr)^G\\ne0\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n \\bigl(V(N\\lambda)\\otimes V(N\\mu)\\otimes V(N\\nu)\\bigr)^G\\ne0.\n\\]"}
